  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 200 PM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nTuesday through Sunday:\n\nEarly Tuesday morning a shortwave will be sliding through \nsouthern MN into southern WI and/or northern IL into the day\nwith an instability gradient likely set up WNW to ESE in that\nsame general vicinity. This will likely be elevated given the\nmorning timing but we cannot rule out something surface based\nand given deep layer shear around 40+ kts severe storms could be\npossible through the early afternoon as this feature tracks\nthrough the region. There is naturally quite a bit of\nuncertainty with this given some much activity through Monday\nthat may affect Tuesday potential but the setup is favorable for\nstrong to severe storms with heavy rain. We do get a sneak peek\nat some the end of the time range of CAMs for this period and a\nthere are several that develop organized convection tracking for\nWI/IL border so that will be something to watch. \n\nBeyond Tuesday uncertainty increases significantly though the\npattern remains the same with ridge to the west and trough to\nthe east that the upper levels indicate several shortwaves\nswinging through throughout the remainder of the week. In\naddition, the instability gradient will likely be in the region\nthroughout the week with decently strong shear. Cannot rule out\nstrong to severe storms at various points the rest of the week\n\nKuroski",
